# CivicLight Linux CPU Miner v2.0.0

This is the first NitroPool Linux release of the CivicLight CPU miner.

The release provides optimized x86_64 binaries for a wide range of Intel and AMD processors, together with an automatic launcher that safely selects the best binary for the detected CPU.

## Release highlights

* Added CivicLight mining support for Linux
* Added automatic CPU detection and binary selection
* Added six optimized CPU builds:

  * Core2
  * AVX
  * AVX2
  * AVX2 with SHA-NI
  * AVX-512
  * AVX-512 with SHA-NI
* Built on Ubuntu 22.04 with GCC 11.4 for broad Linux compatibility
* Added NitroPool AU, EU and US mining support
* Added configurable CPU thread count
* Added coloured CivicLight and NitroPool startup banner
* Added Linux release documentation
* No developer fee

## Download

Download:

`civiclight-miner-linux-x86_64.tar.gz`

Extract the release:

```bash
tar -xzf civiclight-miner-linux-x86_64.tar.gz
cd civiclight-miner-linux-x86_64
```

## Start mining

Replace `YOUR_CIVIC_ADDRESS` with your CivicNet wallet address:

```bash
./civiclight-miner \
  -a civiclight \
  -o stratum+tcp://au.nitropool.net:3032 \
  -u YOUR_CIVIC_ADDRESS.worker \
  -p x
```

Use `-t NUMBER` to control the number of mining threads.

Example using 10 threads:

```bash
./civiclight-miner \
  -a civiclight \
  -o stratum+tcp://au.nitropool.net:3032 \
  -u YOUR_CIVIC_ADDRESS.worker \
  -p x \
  -t 10
```

## NitroPool regions

* Australia: `stratum+tcp://au.nitropool.net:3032`
* Europe: `stratum+tcp://eu.nitropool.net:3032`
* United States: `stratum+tcp://us.nitropool.net:3032`

## Automatic CPU selection

Always start the miner using:

```bash
./civiclight-miner
```

The launcher automatically selects one of the following binaries:

* `cpuminer-core2`
* `cpuminer-avx`
* `cpuminer-avx2`
* `cpuminer-avx2-sha`
* `cpuminer-avx512`
* `cpuminer-avx512-sha`

The selected binary is displayed during startup.

## Hardware testing

The release has been successfully tested on:

* Intel Core i7-8700K

  * 10 mining threads
  * Automatically selected `cpuminer-avx2`
  * Approximately 3.4–3.5 kH/s live mining rate

* Intel Core i5-14400F

  * 12 mining threads
  * Automatically selected `cpuminer-avx2-sha`
  * Approximately 5.7–5.9 kH/s live mining rate

Both systems connected successfully to NitroPool and submitted accepted CivicLight shares with no stale or rejected shares during testing.

## Known issue

CivicLight benchmark mode currently overstates the displayed hashrate.

This does not affect live mining, submitted shares or pool-side hashrate calculations. Use live mining output and pool statistics when evaluating performance.

